    "critique": "The bug is valid and has been successfully reproduced. The Hardware Page Table Walker (HPTW) fails to retain the evaluation of the `Misaligned` signal when it transitions to the `LEAF` state. Because `Misaligned` is strictly tied to `L1_ADR` or `L0_ADR` states (for gigapages and megapages respectively), its value drops to 0 when the FSM enters `LEAF`. Consequently, `OtherPageFault` fails to assert, causing `HPTWUpdateDA` to erroneously become high. This inappropriately drives the FSM into the `UPDATE_PTE` state, mutating the A and D bits in memory before the DTLB can catch the misaligned superpage and raise a page fault. This behavior violates Step 6 of the RISC-V Privileged Architecture Virtual Address Translation process and the exactness requirement of the Svadu extension. The reproducer script accurately demonstrates the divergence between Spike and Wally DUT using valid configuration flags and S-mode trap handlers. Approved."
